      "b64.file.btn.copy": "Copy data URI",
      "b64.file.warning": "Base64 text is about 33% larger than the original file, and very large files can make the browser tab slow — this works best for small-to-medium files like icons, small images, or short documents.",
      "b64.h2.how": "How Base64 encoding works",
      "b64.p.how": "Base64 turns arbitrary binary data (or text) into a string using only 64 printable characters (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, + and /), which makes it safe to embed inside formats that only handle plain text, such as JSON, XML, email (MIME), or a CSS/HTML data URI. This tool uses your browser's built-in btoa/atob functions together with TextEncoder/TextDecoder for correct handling of non-English (UTF-8) text, and FileReader for converting files — no external library is loaded and nothing is uploaded to a server.",
      "b64.h2.when": "When you'd use a Base64 converter",
      "b64.p.when": "Base64 shows up constantly in web development and everyday tech tasks: embedding a small image directly inside CSS or HTML without a separate file request, decoding an API token or JWT payload to see what's inside, reading a Base64-encoded email attachment, or passing binary data through a system (like a URL or JSON field) that only accepts text safely.",

      "uuid.title": "Free UUID / GUID Generator | Code Engineer",
      "uuid.meta": "Generate random UUID v4 / GUID values instantly, one or in bulk, with optional uppercase and no-hyphens formats. Free, runs entirely in your browser, nothing is sent anywhere.",
      "uuid.h1": "UUID / GUID Generator",
      "uuid.desc": "Generate random version-4 UUIDs (also called GUIDs), one at a time or in bulk. Uses your browser's built-in cryptographically secure random number generator — nothing is sent to a server.",
      "uuid.label.count": "How many",
      "uuid.label.uppercase": "Uppercase",
